   "response_text": "Now let me analyze what I've found. Looking at the metrics and training behavior:\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n1. **Training Loss Analysis:**\n   - Initial loss: 0.666571 (epoch 0)\n   - Final loss: 0.653178 (epoch 19)\n   - Total decrease: ~0.013 (~2% improvement)\n   - The loss is decreasing very slowly and monotonically, showing steady but marginal improvement\n\n2. **Validation Accuracy Analysis:**\n   - Oscillates between ~0.83-0.845 throughout training\n   - No clear improvement trend\n   - Ranges from 0.830016 (epoch 18) to 0.845201 (epoch 1)\n   - Appears to have reached a plateau very early\n\n3. **Validation Loss Analysis:**\n   - Also oscillates without clear trend, ranging from 0.491 to 0.549\n   - No convergence pattern\n\n4. **Data Configuration Issue:**\n   - The config shows `label_noise_fraction: 0.33`, meaning 33% of training labels are corrupted\n   - This is a very high amount of label noise, which explains why the model doesn't improve much\n\n5. **Learning Rate:**\n   - LR = 0.01, which is reasonable for Adam optimizer\n   - Batch size = 256, which is reasonable\n\nLet me check if there are any issues with the label noise implementation by looking at the datautil:",
